    "updated_at": "2019-09-23T04:16:50Z",
    "body": "Unfortunately, I can't reproduce this. On my computer, even under the worst-case scenario, the starship initialization time is 40ms, and the prompt draw time is 85ms, which doesn't even get close to one full second. If you allow favorable conditions, it's more like 18 ms for the whole process.\r\n\r\n I'm probably going to need more details from you:\r\n\r\n- What's the launch time of a shell without starship?\r\n- What's the launch time of a shell with starship?\r\n- What else is in your zshrc?\r\n- What Linux are you running? (This makes a difference because different distros have different default rcfiles, which affect timing).\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
