    "body": "> What about an \"instant prompt\" mode similar to Powerlevel10k? I don't know exactly what it does, but I think it defers any other commands in .zshrc somehow so they run in the background.\r\n\r\nThat's what [zsh-defer](https://github.com/romkatv/zsh-defer) does. Instant prompt in Powerlevel10k is different and in most circumstances works much better. It renders prompt manually before zsh is initialized.",
