    "body": "@romkatv Thanks for mentioning zsh-defer, I didn't know about it!\r\n\r\nThe main \"issue\" of Powerlevel10k is that it's zsh-specific. While I definitely agree this gives it an edge since it doesn't need to be generic, I like the idea of cross-shell prompt (especially since I'm moving from Bash right now which has been a nightmare in the last few days of trying to replicate everything). I'm sure zsh-specific functionalities can be included in this project as well if they don't alter the behaviour other than things like speed and things that are unique to that shell.\r\n\r\nThere is also the argument of having to switch shell in some cases and keep the same prompt.\r\n\r\nMy dream would be if the different leading projects (i.e. Powerlevel10k, Starship, Pure) could merge one day in a semi-native way. It's nice that it's already started with the Pure mode in Powerlevel10k :)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
