    "updated_at": "2020-01-13T01:13:04Z",
    "body": "> Why would it be good? Isn't it nice to have a choice of operating systems, shells, terminals and themes?\r\n\r\nOh yes I just meant that it would be nice to have a solution as powerful as as Powerlevel10k but that works on other shells as well (although in degraded mode since zsh has more features).\r\n\r\n> Also, what do you think Pure has that Powerlevel10k doesn't?\r\n\r\nI meant that it used to have a better default style, until Powerlevel10k implemented the \"lean\" and \"pure\" presets. It could be done before but it was not apparent out of the box. My personal favorite is definitely \"lean\".\r\n\r\n> Instant prompt in Powerlevel10k is different and in most circumstances works much better. It renders prompt manually before zsh is initialized.\r\n\r\nAfter testing this I can attest that Powerlevel10k does a much better job since it doesn't block stdin while waiting for initialization to complete.\r\n\r\n@romkatv Thanks for the tips! I actually ended up circling back to Powerlevel10k. It just has some zsh-specific features that are too good to pass on. I think `zsh-defer` is definitely the answer to my original question to solve the delay in starship, even though I won't be needing it.",
